# web3-error-humanizer is an npm library

- Package manager is **npm** (`npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npm ci`). Never yarn.
- Default import is **zero runtime deps**. OpenAI stays on `web3-error-humanizer/ai`.
- Do not bump `package.json` version. semantic-release owns it on `main`.
- Conventional Commits: `feat:` / `fix:` / `docs:` / `chore:`. No Next.js scopes.
- Verify with `npm run test:run`, `npm run lint`, and `npm run build`.
- Prefer `createHumanizer({ chain, patterns, fallbackMessage })` over process-wide `addPattern()` in app examples and tests.
- If you mutate the singleton, call `resetCustomPatterns()` in setup/teardown so the lookup index rebuilds.
- Messages are English. Apps localize via `category` / `matchedKey`. Do not add locale files.
- Do not call `/ai` on a swap confirm path.
- Do not copy Houdini rules: no `@/` imports, no React, no next-intl, no yarn.
